pretation":"Between 2025-11-15 and 2026-11-11 the mean gamma0 VV in the window ranged from -14.0 to -13.1 dB (range 0.8 dB). No change was flagged between consecutive scenes: the surface appears stable at window scale in this period. Between the last two passes, 0.0 % of the pixels (filtered to 50 m) changed by more than 3 dB.","license":"CC BY 4.0 (Sentinel-1 RTC, Planetary Computer)","credit":"Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2025–2026","source":"https://planetarycomputer.microsoft.com/dataset/sentinel-1-rtc","notes":["Orbit used: relative 47 (ascending), VV polarization; 56 acquisitions of that orbit in the period, 26 selected. Other orbits present: 54 descending (56).","Robust site σ_Δ = 0.18 dB; flagged scenes: 0 of 25 pairs.","Fraction of pixels with |Δ| > 3 dB in the last unfiltered pair: 0.098 (speckle-dominated; the published value uses the 5×5 filter).","A backscatter change can be due to soil moisture (rain/dew), sand migration or remobilization, snow/ice or frost, ephemeral vegetation or residual geometry/calibration differences; this product does not attribute causes.","Reanalysis precipitation is a cell-scale estimate (tens of km) and may not reflect local rain."]}
